            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the dispute centers on whether the State waived the affirmative defense of the statute of limitations by failing to raise it earlier and by conceding that the petition was timely."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, the parties argue that a computation error, not a deliberate waiver, led to the State\u2019s late assertion of the limitations defense."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0001",
              "ev-613083aad6ee-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, the case also raises whether a judge may raise a statute\u2011of\u2011limitations defense sua sponte when the State has not."
      }
    ],
