                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the State waived the affirmative defense of limitations by not raising it and by conceding the petition was timely."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0014"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 16,
                "start": 16
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the case should be analyzed under Civil Rules 8 and 12, following Gonzalez and Mayle."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0015"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 17,
                "start": 17
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the State is best positioned to calculate the limitations period; the court should not bear that burden."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0016"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 18,
                "start": 18
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the petitioner seeks a motion to amend the case to address the limitations issue."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-613083aad6ee-0000-0017"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 19,
                "start": 19
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the court should not raise the limitations defense sua sponte when the State has not."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "613083aad6eea4eb66f7f26640905bd27e5ada77d6353c40d3cf2b2c9997fd3b",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-613083aad6ee-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 55,
                "start": 55
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the Eleventh Circuit\u2019s opinion imposes an obligation (a \u201cmust\u201d) rather than a discretionary \u201cmay\u201d regarding the limitations defense."
        }
      ],
